  "A board looks impossible, and isn’t.": "Un tablero parece imposible y no lo es.",
  "Slide a brick and it glides until something stops it. Get every brick out through the gate that matches its colour and the board is clear. A solver cleared all 2,000 boards before any of them shipped, so nothing a player meets is a dead end.": "Desliza un ladrillo y avanza hasta que algo lo detiene. Saca cada ladrillo por la puerta de su color y el tablero queda despejado. Un solucionador despejó los 2000 tableros antes de publicar ninguno, así que nada es un callejón sin salida.",
  "OutBrick has lives and it has advertising, and it says exactly how both work: a life is spent only when an attempt ends without a clear, the first undo on every board is free, and every video is one the player pressed a button to see.": "OutBrick tiene vidas y publicidad y explica exactamente cómo funcionan: solo se consume una vida cuando un intento termina sin despejar, el primer deshacer de cada tablero es gratis y cada vídeo se ve porque el jugador pulsó un botón.",
